<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bunei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1396">1396</a>–<a href="/years/1405">1405</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bunei was king of Chūzan on Okinawa from 1396 to 1405, a son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/satto">Satto</a>. He maintained tribute relations with Ming <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and was formally invested as king by the Ming court. In 1406 he was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-shisho">Shō Shishō</a> and his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sho-hashi">Shō Hashi</a>, who founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-sho-dynasty">First Shō dynasty</a> and later united Okinawa as the Ryukyu Kingdom.</p></div>
